 <h2 class="rv"><span class="px">FAQ</span>Questions</h2>
 <details><summary>How long does one reel take?</summary><p>About 30 minutes to connect everything the first time. After that, a 20-second reel takes 1–2 hours from idea to finished video, most of it waiting for generations.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Is this only for the PS2 style?</summary><p>No. PS2 is one style. The method (character lock, frames before video, Claude checking each step) works for any look. The Pro Kit includes prompt sets for several styles and adds a new one every month.</p></details>
 <details><summary>How much does one reel cost?</summary><p>About $5–7 in Higgsfield credits for a 20-second reel, depending on how many clips it needs. Claude: free to start, Pro for full reels. Most of the savings come from approving 1-credit frames before you pay for video.</p></details>
 <details><summary>I've never used Claude with Higgsfield. Is that a problem?</summary><p>No. The setup is step by step, and the first chapter gets you from zero to your first generated frame.</p></details>
 <details><summary>Do I need to show my face?</summary><p>No. All my reels use AI characters.</p></details>
 <details><summary>How do I get the files?</summary><p>Right after payment you get a link to your personal access page by email. Your files are there, and every update and new style lands there too, so it never goes out of date.</p></details>
